PROJECT: AUTO-DETECTING UNIVERSAL INVITATION EDITOR
Act as a senior frontend engineer, UI/UX designer, typography specialist, SVG rendering expert and product architect.
Build a premium, commercially usable invitation customization website for a business that sells editable digital invitations on Etsy. This is a real product, not a student project, dashboard or landing page. Right now we are in testing mode with a dummy design. Later, real Etsy designs will be dropped in without code changes.
1. Business model and customer journey
1.  A customer buys a digital invitation on Etsy.
2.  Etsy delivers a PDF with one unique URL, for example https://ourwebsite.netlify.app/editor/wildflower-001.
3.  The customer opens it. The site loads only that one design.
4.  They type their details, see a live preview, restyle what the design allows, and download a print-ready PDF or PNG.
No account, no login, no technical knowledge. Many customers use phones, so mobile is first-class.
2. Core principle: ONE ENGINE, AUTO-DETECTION, ZERO DESIGN-SPECIFIC CODE
Every design is different (fields, positions, fonts, colors, size, orientation). Therefore:
• A template is ONE file: design.svg. The engine reads the SVG and detects everything editable by itself.
• config.json is optional. If present, it only overrides or refines what was detected (labels, limits, allowed fonts). A template with no config must still work.
• Nothing in src/ may mention a specific design. Adding a design = drop in a folder with design.svg, run the inspector, deploy. If an ordinary design needs a code change, that is an engine bug: fix the engine.
• The edit panel is generated from what was detected. Controls for things the design does not contain never appear.
3. NO template gallery
This is not a marketplace. Do not build a template gallery, library, "change template" button, public template registry, or any code that fetches more than the requested template.
• /editor/:templateId is the only real customer page.
• / shows a neutral page: logo and "Please open the personal link from your Etsy instruction PDF." plus a Help link. No design previews.
• Unknown IDs show a friendly Not Found page that does not list other templates.
• Add <meta name="robots" content="noindex">.
• The only exception is the dev-only inspector (section 9), available only in development builds or with an explicit build flag, never in production.
4. Technology stack
• React + Vite (JavaScript), React Router, modern CSS. No backend, no database, no accounts, no payments, no paid services.
